# Pages were being cached for ten minutes, so pressing refresh could hand
# back the version from before a change -- which wasted a good deal of
# everyone's time. no-cache does not stop the browser keeping a copy; it
# makes it ask first, and an unchanged file comes back as a 304.
#
# A rule for /assets/* was tried alongside this one and both applied, which
# produced "no-cache, public, max-age=31536000, immutable" on every asset.
# Scripts and stylesheets already carry a content hash in their URL, so a
# revalidation on them is cheap and the long cache was not worth a
# self-contradicting header.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
